.TH LAC 1 "August 2026" "Linux Admin Center 1.2.0-alpha1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lac \- modular Linux desktop administration toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lac
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Linux Admin Center (LAC) provides an interactive terminal interface and
command-line options for common Linux desktop administration tasks.
.PP
Run
.B lac
without an option to open the interactive menu. Exactly one command-line option
may be supplied at a time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " --help"
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-v , " --version"
Show version information.
.TP
.BR \-i , " --system-info"
Show system information.
.TP
.BR \-n , " --network-info"
Show network information.
.TP
.BR \-r , " --network-diagnostics"
Show read-only network diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-d , " --hardware-diagnostics"
Show read-only hardware diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-g , " --gaming-readiness"
Show the gaming readiness overview.
.TP
.BR \-G , " --gaming-diagnostics"
Show detailed gaming diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-e , " --service-health"
Show service and boot health information.
.TP
.BR \-S , " --self-check"
Check the LAC runtime, launchers, configuration access and dependencies.
.TP
.BR \-u , " --check-updates"
Check for available system package updates.
.TP
.BR \-c , " --cleanup-report"
Show a read-only system cleanup report.
.SH CONFIGURATION
LAC reads system configuration from
.I /etc/lac/lac.conf
and user configuration from an explicit
.B LAC_USER_CONFIG
path, the XDG configuration directory, or
.IR ~/.config/lac/lac.conf .
.PP
The packaged example configuration is installed under
.IR /usr/share/linux-admin-center/lac.conf.example .
.SH PACKAGE MANAGEMENT
Debian package installations are managed through
.BR apt (8)
and
.BR dpkg (1).
The package intentionally does not install a
.B lac-uninstall
command. Remove it with:
.PP
.nf
sudo apt remove linux-admin-center
.fi
.PP
Configuration under
.I /etc/lac
and user configuration are not removed by that operation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/lac
Installed command.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/linux-admin-center/
LAC runtime files.
.TP
.I /usr/share/linux-admin-center/
Shared files and example configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/lac/lac.conf
Optional system-wide configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
